              "gh:imagePrompt": "Manga panel illustration to be published in Weekly Shounen Jump (週刊少年ジャンプ) — each panel must read as a STANDALONE artwork, monochrome with screen tones, single full-bleed image. SCENE SUBJECT (the panel's main beat): Nei enters the classroom. Visual to render: Nei enters the classroom confidently, holding a bag of donut in one hand. The room is filled with sunlight falling on Ren's sleeping form at the desk. Nei's expression is a mix of mischief and determination.. KEY PROPS in scene (must be visible and recognizable, integrated into the composition): donut bag, Kommetcon donut. Shot framing: Wide. Composition: rule-of-thirds with focal character on golden ratio line; at least one prop in mid-ground; hand position and body language must be intentional and readable; depth of field with softened background. Characters in frame (each must be visually distinct): Nei [FOCUS] (in-frame 1/2) / Ren (in-frame 2/2). Compositional focus is on Nei. Required physical signals (must be visible in the rendered image): Nei: bright eyes, slight smirk. Emotional tone: quiet. Style: detailed atmospheric establishing illustration — full environmental detail with weather/light condition, scenic depth, architectural specificity, texture-rich screen tones. Inspired by 天野こずえ Aria's establishing pages — peaceful, world-grounding detail. Story continuity — preceding beat: Nei approaches the classroom. / following beat: Nei calls out to Ren.. The panel must visually connect with these beats. Character face-identity references are supplied as input images IN THIS ORDER: (1) Nei. Use each reference ONLY for face identity (face shape, eye design, hairstyle, age impression) of the named character — do NOT copy reference clothing, pose, or background. Apply standard Japanese school uniform appropriate to the setting and the pose described. ABSOLUTE: NO text, NO speech bubbles, NO captions, NO labels, NO storyboard frames or scene numbers in the rendered image.",
