          "gh:imagePrompt": "ONE SINGLE manga-style illustration filling the entire image, black-and-white monochrome with screen tones. NOT a manga page with multiple sub-frames — just ONE single contiguous illustration. Fictional original characters for Weekly Shounen Jump style fiction publication, entirely fictional and not based on any real persons. SCENE SUBJECT (the panel's main beat): Feeling reassured. Visual to render: Yuto sits back, a sigh of relief escaped from his lips as his expression turns to a small, hopeful smile, feeling thankful for the swift response.. KEY PROPS in scene (must be visible and recognizable, integrated into the composition): smartphone. Shot framing: Medium. Composition: rule-of-thirds with focal character on golden ratio line; at least one prop in mid-ground; hand position and body language must be intentional and readable; depth of field with softened background. Characters in frame (each must be visually distinct): Yuto [FOCUS]. Compositional focus is on Yuto. Required physical signals (must be visible in the rendered image): Yuto: sighing, gentle smile, slightly closed eyes. Emotional tone: emotional. Style: cinematic film-like medium shot — rule-of-thirds composition, layered foreground/midground/background with depth of field, set dressing visible, characters staged with intentional spacing, soft tonal gradients. Inspired by 攻殻機動隊 (押井守 film aesthetics) calm dialogue scenes and Aria's tonal medium shots. Story continuity — preceding beat: Reading the response. / following beat: Considering the implications of the positive reply.. The panel must visually connect with these beats. Character face-identity references are supplied as input images IN THIS ORDER: (1) Yuto. Use each reference ONLY for face identity (face shape, eye design, hairstyle, age impression) of the named character — do NOT copy reference clothing, pose, or background. Apply standard Japanese school uniform appropriate to the setting and the pose described. ABSOLUTE: ONE seamless full-bleed image only. NO sub-panels, NO panel dividers, NO multi-frame layout, NO text, NO speech bubbles, NO captions, NO labels, NO storyboard frames or scene numbers.",
