          "gh:imagePrompt": "ONE SINGLE manga-style illustration filling the entire image, black-and-white monochrome with screen tones. NOT a manga page with multiple sub-frames — just ONE single contiguous illustration. Fictional original characters for Weekly Shounen Jump style fiction publication, entirely fictional and not based on any real persons. SCENE SUBJECT (the panel's main beat): Nei's Sudden Entrance. Visual to render: Medium anime-action shot: Ren is caught mid-rise, カバン slung over one shoulder, pausing as Nei makes a decisive entrance into the room. Nei steps in with confident momentum, cleanly interrupting Ren's motion and drawing the scene's focus to their shared tension.. KEY PROPS in scene (must be visible and recognizable, integrated into the composition): カバン. Shot framing: Medium. Composition: rule-of-thirds with focal character on golden ratio line; at least one prop in mid-ground; hand position and body language must be intentional and readable; depth of field with softened background. Characters in frame (each must be visually distinct): Ren (in-frame 1/2) / Nei (in-frame 2/2). Required physical signals (must be visible in the rendered image): Ren: wide-eyed surprise, lifted brows / Nei: grounded stance, steady gaze. Emotional tone: action. Style: dynamic shounen action — exaggerated foreshortening, motion lines streaking from the focal character, speed effects, Dutch angle, impact stars/burst effects, halftone speed dust. Inspired by 岸本斉史 Naruto fight panels and 尾田栄一郎 One Piece battle compositions. Story continuity — preceding beat: Ren is getting ready to leave. / following beat: Nei makes a request to Ren, urging him to help someone.. The panel must visually connect with these beats. Character face-identity references are supplied as input images IN THIS ORDER: (1) Ren, (2) Nei. Use each reference ONLY for face identity (face shape, eye design, hairstyle, age impression) of the named character — do NOT copy reference clothing, pose, or background. Apply standard Japanese school uniform appropriate to the setting and the pose described. ABSOLUTE: ONE seamless full-bleed image only. NO sub-panels, NO panel dividers, NO multi-frame layout, NO text, NO speech bubbles, NO captions, NO labels, NO storyboard frames or scene numbers.",
