          "gh:imagePrompt": "ONE SINGLE manga-style illustration filling the entire image, black-and-white monochrome with screen tones. NOT a manga page with multiple sub-frames — just ONE single contiguous illustration. Fictional original characters for Weekly Shounen Jump style fiction publication, entirely fictional and not based on any real persons. SCENE SUBJECT (the panel's main beat): Success confirmed. Visual to render: Ren stands with a slight smile, offering a thumb-up to Yuto. Yuto looks up, reflecting Ren's positivity.. Shot framing: Close Up. Composition: head and shoulders frame; expression-driving features (eyes + mouth) sharply rendered; subtle background bokeh; one expressive physical signal required; lighting indicates the emotional motivation. Characters in frame (each must be visually distinct): Ren [FOCUS] (in-frame 1/2) / Yuto (in-frame 2/2). Compositional focus is on Ren. Required physical signals (must be visible in the rendered image): Ren: thumb-up, smiling eyes / Yuto: relieved sigh, nodding. Emotional tone: triumph. Style: cinematic emotional close-up — extreme depth of field, rim lighting carving the focal character's silhouette, dramatic chiaroscuro shadow play, eyes as the dominant focal element with sharp catchlights, atmospheric particles. Inspired by 攻殻機動隊 (士郎正宗) quiet contemplation panels and One Piece emotional close-ups. Story continuity — preceding beat: Yuto finishes setting up passwords. / following beat: Next steps await.. The panel must visually connect with these beats. Character face-identity references are supplied as input images IN THIS ORDER: (1) Ren. Use each reference ONLY for face identity (face shape, eye design, hairstyle, age impression) of the named character — do NOT copy reference clothing, pose, or background. Apply standard Japanese school uniform appropriate to the setting and the pose described. ABSOLUTE: ONE seamless full-bleed image only. NO sub-panels, NO panel dividers, NO multi-frame layout, NO text,