              "gh:imagePrompt": "Fictional manga panel illustration of original characters created for a fiction publication (Weekly Shounen Jump style). All characters are entirely fictional and not based on any real persons. Black-and-white monochrome with screen tones, single full-bleed image, each panel reads as a standalone artwork. SCENE SUBJECT (the panel's main beat): Transformed classroom. Visual to render: A wide establishing view of the classroom shows reality shifting into a surreal black-and-blue wireframe layer, with the ワイヤーフレームの黒板, 窓, 机, and classmates all rendered in geometric outlines. The effect creates a dual-view atmosphere, as if the familiar room has been overlaid with an uncanny digital blueprint, setting an ominous tone around the shared group reaction.. KEY PROPS in scene (must be visible and recognizable, integrated into the composition): ワイヤーフレームの黒板, 窓, 机. Shot framing: Wide. Composition: rule-of-thirds with focal character on golden ratio line; at least one prop in mid-ground; hand position and body language must be intentional and readable; depth of field with softened background. Characters in frame (each must be visually distinct): Ren (in-frame 1/5) / クラスメイト (in-frame 2/5) / Mei (in-frame 3/5) / Akira (in-frame 4/5) / Saki (in-frame 5/5). Required physical signals (must be visible in the rendered image): クラスメイト: fixed wide gaze, stunned expression / Mei: lifted brows, focused look of disbelief / Akira: hands pressed to head, leaning back in alarm / Saki: arms raised in reflex, stepping back with tense posture. Emotional tone: ominous. Style: detailed atmospheric establishing illustration — full environmental detail with weather/light condition, scenic depth, architectural specificity, texture-rich screen tones. Inspired by 天野こずえ Aria's establishing pages — peaceful, world-grounding detail. Story continuity — preceding beat: Reality remains intact. / following beat: Everyone is startled by the transformation.. The panel must visually connect with these beats. Character face-identity references are supplied as input images IN THIS ORDER: (1) Ren, (2) Mei. Use each reference ONLY for face identity (face shape, eye design, hairstyle, age impression) of the named character — do NOT copy reference clothing, pose, or background. Apply standard Japanese school uniform appropriate to the setting and the pose described. ABSOLUTE: NO text, NO speech bubbles, NO captions, NO labels, NO storyboard frames or scene numbers in the rendered image.",
